{
    "title": "Pinochle",
    "description": "Pinochle is believed to have originated in Europe and became popular in the United States, particularly among German immigrants. Pinochle is a trick-taking game, similar to bridge and euchre, and it requires both skill and strategy to win.\r\n\r\nIf you're a beginner, don't worry. We have comprehensive game tutorials prepared to help you quickly become proficient and master Pinochle.\r\n\r\nIn our product, besides the classic four-player mode, we also offer many popular gameplay options for you to choose from.\r\n\r\n---For the use of playing cards, aside from the traditional 48-card deck, you can also opt for a 40-card deck by \u201cRemoving all the 9s\u201d, or choose the \u201cDouble Deck\u201d option.\r\n\r\n---For the number of players, in addition to the four-player team matches, there is also the option for three individuals to compete separately.\r\n\r\n---For the scoring of each card, whether it's the traditional 11-10-4-3-2-0 scoring or the popular 10-10-10-0-0-0 scoring, it can also be adjusted based on your preference.\r\n\r\nOur product doesn't require an internet connection to play. You can compete against strategic AI opponents. We also offer a variety of tablecloths and card styles for you to choose from.\r\n\r\nWhat are you waiting for? Download our product now and step into the world of Pinochle!",
    "descriptionHTML": "Pinochle is believed to have originated in Europe and became popular in the United States, particularly among German immigrants. Pinochle is a trick-taking game, similar to bridge and euchre, and it requires both skill and strategy to win.<br><br>If you&#39;re a beginner, don&#39;t worry. We have comprehensive game tutorials prepared to help you quickly become proficient and master Pinochle.<br><br>In our product, besides the classic four-player mode, we also offer many popular gameplay options for you to choose from.<br><br>---For the use of playing cards, aside from the traditional 48-card deck, you can also opt for a 40-card deck by \u201cRemoving all the 9s\u201d, or choose the \u201cDouble Deck\u201d option.<br><br>---For the number of players, in addition to the four-player team matches, there is also the option for three individuals to compete separately.<br><br>---For the scoring of each card, whether it&#39;s the traditional 11-10-4-3-2-0 scoring or the popular 10-10-10-0-0-0 scoring, it can also be adjusted based on your preference.<br><br>Our product doesn&#39;t require an internet connection to play. You can compete against strategic AI opponents. We also offer a variety of tablecloths and card styles for you to choose from.<br><br>What are you waiting for? Download our product now and step into the world of Pinochle!",
    "summary": "You can play classic pinochle, double deck, and more modes here!",
